Q: TimelineView or timer in .common RunLoop mode causing Menu with .buttonStyle(.plain) to flicker A: <p>Perhaps your best workaround is what you mentioned in the post:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If .buttonStyle(.plain) is removed from the Menu, this issue disappears.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It is possible to apply quite a lot of styling to the menu button without setting a <code>.buttonStyle</code>. In particular:</p>
<ul>
<li>use <code>.menuIndicator(.hidden)</code> to hide the arrow</li>
<li>the shape can be changed by applying a clip shape.</li>
</ul>
<p>However, you may not be able to change the padding or the darkening effect when the menu is tapped.</p>
<p>Here is a simple example:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>Menu {
    Menu {
        Button(&quot;Item&quot;) {}
    } label: {
        Text(&quot;Submenu&quot;)
    }
} label: {
    Text(&quot;Menu&quot;)
        .font(.title2)
        .fontWeight(.semibold)
        .foregroundStyle(.red)
}
.menuIndicator(.hidden)
.background {
    Capsule()
        .fill(.yellow.opacity(0.8))
        .strokeBorder(.red, lineWidth: 2)
}
.clipShape(.capsule)
</code></pre>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/wjLjaSAY.gif" alt="Animation" /></p>
<hr />
<p>For more elaborate styling, you could consider converting the label content to an image.</p>
<ul>
<li>An <code>ImageRenderer</code> can be used for this.</li>
<li>This lets you use almost any styling you like, except that there is still a light gray shade applied to the label and this is darkened when the menu is tapped.</li>
<li>Use <code>.accessibilityLabel</code> to set a readable label, for the benefit of VoiceOver.</li>
</ul>
<p>Here is an example of how this approach can be used:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>private func content2Image&lt;C: View&gt;(content: () -&gt; C) -&gt; Image {
    if let nsImage = ImageRenderer(content: content()).nsImage {
        Image(nsImage: nsImage)
    } else {
        Image(systemName: &quot;exclamationmark.triangle&quot;)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>Menu {
    Menu {
        Button(&quot;Item&quot;) {}
    } label: {
        Text(&quot;Submenu&quot;)
    }
} label: {
    content2Image {
        HStack {
            HStack {
                Text(&quot;Menu&quot;)
                Image(systemName: &quot;line.3.horizontal&quot;)
                    .foregroundStyle(.orange)
            }
            .font(.title2)
            .fontWeight(.semibold)
            .foregroundStyle(.red)
            .imageScale(.large)
            .padding(.horizontal, 20)
            .padding(.vertical, 10)
        }
    }
}
.menuIndicator(.hidden)
.accessibilityLabel(&quot;Menu&quot;)
.background {
    Capsule()
        .fill(.yellow.opacity(0.8))
        .strokeBorder(.red, lineWidth: 2)
}
.clipShape(.capsule)
</code></pre>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/ZCeC6ymS.gif" alt="Animation" /></p>
